{{feat
|type=class
|prereq=[[wizard]] 1, [[sorcerer]] 1
|desc=A character with this feat may [[summon]] a [[familiar]] once per day. If the familiar dies, the character suffers 1[[d6]] [[magical damage]], but may summon the familiar again on the following [[day]].
|use=selected
|icon=ife_familiar.gif
|class1=sorcerer
|class2=wizard
}}

The available familiars are [[bat (familiar)|bat]], [[eyeball (familiar)|eyeball]], [[faerie dragon (familiar)|faerie dragon]], [[fire mephit (familiar)|fire mephit]], [[hell hound (familiar)|hell hound]], [[ice mephit (familiar)|ice mephit]], [[imp (familiar)|imp]], [[panther (familiar)|panther]], [[pixie (familiar)|pixie]], [[pseudodragon (familiar)|pseudodragon]], and [[raven (familiar)|raven]].

== Notes ==

* This ability targets the summoner (unlike summoning spells, which target the ground).
* Multiclassing sorcerer and wizard will not give the character two familiars, but those [[class level]]s do [[stack]] when determining the level of the familiar upon summoning (as opposed to the level-up process, where the familiar appears to be the level of the selected class).

